# Names only, never a value. Copy this file to .env at the repo root and fill it in; .env is ignored by
# git. The real environment wins over the file.
#
# ascc itself has no settings: it reads a policy file and an agent registry from the repo, writes its
# audit log next to them, holds no credential and calls no API.
#
# The development stack in deploy/compose/ takes every secret it has from here, and won't start with one
# missing. Use a long random value for each, letters and digits only. `openssl rand -hex 32` makes one, and
# the seal key must be exactly that: 32 random bytes as 64 hex digits.
ASCC_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
ASCC_KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
ASCC_OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY=
ASCC_OPENBAO_ROOT_TOKEN=
